==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|átta|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{recons|ahtōu|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{recons|oḱtṓw|lang=ine-pro}}. Compare Norwegian {{term|åtte|lang=no}}, Swedish {{term|åtta|lang=sv}}, Danish {{term|otte|lang=da}}.

===Number===
'''átta''' {{indecl}}

# '''[[eight]]'''; the cardinal number after [[sjö#Icelandic|sjö]] and before [[níu#Icelandic|níu]].

====Related terms====
* {{qualifier|ordinal form}} [[áttundi]] {{m}}, [[áttunda]] {{f|n}}

